        "original_id": "7b34e23c-2941-542a-b6d7-ba4f3aaeb705",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robbie Coltrane, J. K. Rowling, Tony Forsyth, Emile Charles, Bruce Payne\n- Characters: Rubeus Hagrid, Valentin Dmitrovich Zukovsky, Dr. Eddie \"Fitz\" Fitzgerald, Annabelle\n- Works: Harry Potter, GoldenEye, The World Is Not Enough, Cracker, The Fruit Machine, Wonderland\n- Topics: acting, authorship\n\nFacts:\n- Robbie Coltrane was born Anthony Robert McMillan on 30 March 1950 and is a Scottish actor and author.\n- In 1988, The Fruit Machine, released in the United States as Wonderland, starred Tony Forsyth, Emile Charles, Bruce Payne, and Robbie Coltrane, who played Annabelle.\n- During the 1990s, Robbie Coltrane played Dr. Eddie \"Fitz\" Fitzgerald in the British TV series Cracker.\n- Robbie Coltrane played Valentin Dmitrovich Zukovsky in the James Bond films GoldenEye and The World Is Not Enough.\n- Robbie Coltrane is known for playing Rubeus Hagrid in the Harry Potter films.\n- Rubeus Hagrid is a fictional character in the Harry Potter book series written by J. K. Rowling.",
